## 1. Product in one paragraph

A homeowner or small contractor in Pune enters built-up area, floors, location zone, quality tier and (optionally) a budget. BuildSmart AI returns: a **predicted total construction cost with an honest low-high range and confidence label**, a **9-category cost breakdown**, **material recommendations per category** that fit the budget, and a **downloadable PDF**. Users keep a **history of projects and estimates**. Every number is traceable to a model version and a dataset version, and the product is upfront about what it is (a preliminary estimate, not a quotation).

---

## 2. Non-negotiable principles

These rules apply to every human and every AI agent touching this repo.

1. **No invented data.** Never fabricate prices, rates, datasets, benchmarks, metrics, citations, URLs, or library APIs. If a value is unknown, leave a clearly marked `TODO(data)` and raise it in [§23](#23-open-decisions-for-the-team).
2. **Metrics are measured, not promised.** Any accuracy figure shown in the UI, PDF, README or viva must be produced by the evaluation script and stored in the model card. Targets in this document are *gates*, not claims.
3. **Provenance on every data row.** Each training/reference row carries `source`, `source_date`, and `data_type` (`real_project` | `published_rate_derived` | `synthetic`). Synthetic data is always labelled as such in the model card and in the UI "Methodology" page.
4. **Verify before using a library.** Before writing code against a dependency, read its current docs or installed source. Use latest stable versions, pin them in lockfiles, and do not rely on memory of APIs.
5. **Preliminary, not professional.** The product never claims to replace an engineer's or contractor's quotation. The disclaimer appears on the results page and in every PDF.
6. **Reproducibility.** Given a data version + config + seed, `make train` reproduces the same model artifact and metrics.
7. **No scope creep.** Out-of-scope items in [§3](#3-scope) are not built, even if easy.
8. **Security by default.** Follow [§14](#14-authentication-and-security). No secrets in git. No `eval`, no unsafe deserialisation of user data.
9. **Ask, don't assume.** When a requirement is ambiguous, stop and ask. Write the decision into `docs/decisions/` (one short ADR per decision).

---

## 3. Scope

### In scope
- Residential buildings only: small and medium houses (independent houses / bungalows / row houses).
- Pune and surrounding areas, grouped into a **small number of cost zones** (see [§8.4](#84-location-zones)).
- Standard material **categories and grades**, not commercial brands.
- Preliminary cost prediction, range, breakdown, material recommendations, dashboard, PDF, saved history.

### Out of scope (do not build)
- Structural/civil engineering calculations, load analysis, concrete mix design.
- Floor plans, blueprints, 3D models.
- Live supplier/market APIs and binding contractor quotations.
- Government approvals, permits, legal compliance.
- Commercial/industrial buildings, high-rises, renovations.
- Native mobile apps (web must be fully responsive).

---

## 4. Users and core user stories

**Primary:** homeowners, first-time builders. **Secondary:** small contractors, civil engineering students, real estate consultants.

| ID | Story | Priority |
|----|-------|----------|
| US-1 | As a user I can register, log in, log out, and stay logged in securely. | Must |
| US-2 | I can enter project details and get a cost estimate with a range. | Must |
| US-3 | I see a 9-category cost breakdown as chart and table. | Must |
| US-4 | I get material recommendations that fit my quality tier and budget. | Must |
| US-5 | I can download a professional PDF of any estimate. | Must |
| US-6 | I can see, rename, re-estimate, and delete my projects. | Must |
| US-7 | I can compare two estimates of the same project (e.g., Standard vs Premium). | Should |
| US-8 | I can reset my password by email. | Should |
| US-9 | I can read how estimates are produced (methodology, data sources, limits). | Must |
| US-10 | I can try a quick estimate without an account (rate-limited). | Could |

MoSCoW rule: **all Musts ship before any Should starts.**

