## 20. Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|--------|------------|
| Too little real cost data | **High** | **High** | Start collection Week 1; publish real-vs-derived composition; cap confidence label; report real-only accuracy; frame output as preliminary |
| Model looks accurate only because data was generated by a formula | High | High | Separate real validation set; never tune on it; Baseline A comparison |
| Source URLs/datasets in synopsis don't say what we assume | Medium | High | Open and verify each one; log in `DATA_SOURCES.md`; fix references before final submission |
| Free-tier hosting cold starts / limits | Medium | Medium | Measure early; waking-up UX; fallback provider |
| Scope creep (3D, live prices, mobile) | Medium | Medium | §3 is binding; Could items only after Musts |
| Auth implemented insecurely | Medium | High | §14 checklist, tests for rotation/IDOR, code review |
| AI agent hallucinates APIs or numbers | Medium | High | §2 contract, small phases, tests-first, human review of each PR |
| Team member bandwidth | Medium | Medium | Clear ownership per phase; pairing on ML and auth |
| Training/serving skew | Low | High | Single sklearn Pipeline artifact; parity test |
| Price drift makes model stale | Certain over time | Medium | Data-version dates in UI; manual retraining procedure documented |

---

## 21. Definition of Done / ship checklist

**Functional**
- [ ] Register, login, refresh, logout, profile work; refresh rotation and reuse detection tested.
- [ ] Create project → estimate → results → PDF → re-estimate → delete works end-to-end on production.
- [ ] Estimate always shows a range, confidence label, disclaimer, model and data version.
- [ ] 9 categories always sum exactly to the total.
- [ ] Material recommendations are explainable and respond to tier and budget.

**ML**
- [ ] Model card complete; real-data metrics recorded; Baseline A comparison included.
- [ ] Invariant tests pass; out-of-range inputs rejected.
- [ ] Methodology page states data composition and limitations truthfully.

**Quality**
- [ ] CI green; coverage thresholds met; E2E passes against the production build.
- [ ] Lighthouse ≥ 90 (performance, accessibility, best practices) on key pages; axe clean.
- [ ] Works at 360 px width; keyboard-only flow completes an estimate.

**Security**
- [ ] §14.2 fully checked; no secrets in history; scans clean or exceptions documented.

**Operations**
- [ ] Deployed on Vercel + Railway/Render with HTTPS; migrations automated; backups on and restore tested; health checks green.
- [ ] `.env.example` complete; fresh-clone setup ≤ 10 minutes verified by a teammate who did not write it.

**Academic**
- [ ] README, synopsis, tracker, poster and demo all tell the same story and quote the same numbers (from the model card).
- [ ] Every reference and URL verified.

